# eon-gkeae — cause

**Eon's guarded Nushell Starship activation loads an overlay inside a nested block. With pinned Nu 0.113.1, directory completion then keeps using the shell's startup directory after `cd`.** The command itself and the displayed prompt use the correct current directory. At startup, or after returning to the startup directory, the two views agree and the failure is hidden.

Owner: Eon's Nix shell adapter, `nix/shell-environment.nix:88-105`, specifically line 101:

```nu
if ( ... default-prompt guards ... ) {
  try {
    overlay use ($_eon_shell_init | path join starship-nu)
  } catch {|error| ... }
}
```

The observable cause is demonstrated without any other integration: loading a trivial `export-env { $env.PROBE_OVERLAY = true }` module inside the same `if`/`try` shape reproduces empty completion in a new directory and erroneous completion of a name found only in the startup directory. Loading the overlay at top level does not. Scoped `source` and `use` of the real Starship initializer also do not. These are controls against the actual pinned binary, not an assumption based on documentation.

The underlying scoped-overlay behavior is reproducible in upstream pinned Nushell alone; it does not require Eon, Venus, Orbit, or Starship. Eon introduces it through its activation shape and can avoid it locally. Classification for this verification is **REPRODUCED, Eon integration trigger with an upstream scoped-overlay mechanism**, not an unqualified upstream-only verdict.

Primary source corroboration: [Nushell directory_completions.rs at the exact pin](https://github.com/nushell/nushell/blob/7b7df4aa68e957cf38b9d8157c35fa7523f44a6d/crates/nu-cli/src/completions/directory_completions.rs#L31) obtains the search CWD from `working_set.permanent_state.current_work_dir()`. [arg_value_completion.rs](https://github.com/nushell/nushell/blob/7b7df4aa68e957cf38b9d8157c35fa7523f44a6d/crates/nu-cli/src/completions/arg_value_completion.rs#L207) routes directory arguments to that completer. Read-only copies are under `../evidence/upstream/`. The exact internal env/overlay propagation defect has not been fully traced, and no claim is made about its status in newer Nu versions.

Carapace is not the cause: its toggle and removing the external closure leave the failure, and the trivial-overlay case contains no Carapace. Zoxide does not alias `cd` in the shipped setup. Atuin and mise are also unnecessary to reproduce. Plain pinned Nu completes in the new directory. Existing user configuration can avoid or independently produce completion problems, but none was needed for this reproduction.

This explains a report that says completion fails in a managed pane but omits the earlier directory change. It does **not** establish that Ronald's exact environment has this cause; the overseer can ask him to compare immediately after opening a pane, after `cd`, and with `[shell] starship = false` in a fresh managed pane.

